2026-09-08,windows,gtk4,P47,ok,-,window,default,"symbols: NOT the same as winui on the same machine, which is why this is a separate row. sync falls back to its textFallback and draws as Sy... rather than an icon. That is the measured GTK behaviour, not a defect: probing GTK 4.22.4 on 2026-09-07 found sync-synchronizing-symbolic absent from the 138 icons GTK bundles, and adwaita-icon-theme is what would supply it. The fallback firing is the feature working. Recording this per backend because one 'Windows passed' row would have hidden a real difference between the two backends that ship on the same platform"
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P15-DARK,ok,ok,window,unrecorded,"CORRECTION to this morning's diagnosis, which called P15 a stale-coordinates case. It was not: the sweep was launching P15 for P15-DARK's action file. HARNESS DEFECT, fixed 2026-09-08. All four sweep scripts derived the app with app=${base%%-*}, which truncates at the first hyphen -- right for P7-select-a-list-row and wrong for P15-DARK-the-override-survives-a-tap. Both variant apps exist (testapp/P15-DARK.swift, testapp/P17-DOE.swift), so this was the wrong file rather than a missing one, and the run reported cleanly. It was invisible from the results because captures are named after the SCENARIO: P15-DARK-...-control.png held a picture of P15, and the taps landed on blank space in an app nobody meant to test. Now resolves the longest prefix that names a real .swift. Fixed in verify_effect_ios.zsh, verify_effect_android.zsh, verify_replay_android.zsh and sweep_android.zsh. Re-run correctly: the five points the action file pinned on 2026-09-02 all read (0,0,0) again, so the dark override is genuinely in force, and body text is (255,255,255). Result: no visible change, which is this scenario's PASS -- the button's action is empty and the file's whole claim is that a tap leaves every pixel where it was. It joins P6 and P42 as press-nothing-by-design"
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P17-DOE,ok,ok,window,unrecorded,Re-run after the same harness fix; it had been driven against P17. both-directions-clip: 551262 px changed over 3 actions
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P15-DARK,ok,ok,window,unrecorded,"FINDING, from a pin the action file placed deliberately. It recorded the A button label as exactly (0,122,255) = #007AFF on 2026-09-02 and said it was written down 'so a later change is visible'. It is now (0,145,255) = #0091FF, and #007AFF appears zero times. That is neither the old value nor UIColor.systemBlue resolved in a dark trait collection (#0A84FF), so it is a third thing and not yet explained. Recorded, not chased: the pin did its job and the cause is separate work"
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P17,ok,ok,window,unrecorded,"FINDING 1 -- the iOS action files were measured 68 minutes before the layout changed under them. 978f0e0b wrote all 48 at 11:23 on 2026-09-02; bee0fbba hosted the root child in a scroll view at 12:31 the same day, and its own message says fourteen of the forty-six apps are wider than a phone and that it shifts content by -origin. So the coordinates did not drift: a known change whose purpose was to move content invalidated them an hour after they were written. This is the same cause behind P5, P7 and P33, which were re-measured earlier today and now work"
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P17,ok,ok,window,unrecorded,"FINDING 2, CORRECTED the same day. P17's content is offset right by about 260 pt -- measured x 260..393 while P15, P46 and P47 start at 12..16. The cause is in RootScrollHost.contentBounds, which seeds its box with CGRect(origin: .zero, ...) so box.minX can never be positive; content.frame.origin = -box.minX therefore always shifts RIGHT, by however far the content extends to the left. For P17 that is 260 pt. **The first version of this row said it does not scroll, and that was wrong.** The probe scrolled LEFT, which clamps at zero on content already flush left. Scrolling RIGHT moves 618,358 px, so the host works -- P10 moves 287,205 px the same way. What remains true is the 260 pt of blank screen on the left and that the design's own left edge is only reachable by scrolling"
2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P17,-,-,-,unrecorded,"FINDING 3 -- P17's action file is still NOT re-measured, and the reason narrowed. Not because the layout is unscrollable, which was wrong, but because the 260 pt right shift is a defect in RootScrollHost rather than a property of the app: coordinates measured now would encode the shift and have to be measured again when it is fixed. The mechanism goes first"
